From: HakiOS <hakios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0006/6] makedefs: disable -Wreserved-identifier

This is the first warning that actually stops the compile. With
-Weverything + -Werror, clang promotes

    BUILD/obj/EXPORT_HDRS/bsd/arm/_types.h:15:33: error:
      identifier '__int8_t' is reserved because it starts with '__'
      [-Werror,-Wreserved-identifier]

and every typedef in that header becomes an error: one object file
reported "156 errors generated", all of them this same diagnostic.

-Wreserved-identifier did not exist when XNU 8020 was written (2021).
The kernel's own headers legitimately use __-prefixed names, so the
warning can never be satisfied here. Disabled in the block that already
exists for exactly this purpose ("When a new clang has new warnings
disable them here until the kernel is fixed").

---
--- a/makedefs/MakeInc.def
+++ b/makedefs/MakeInc.def
@@ -180,7 +180,8 @@
 	-Wno-error=enum-enum-conversion \
 	-Wno-error=c99-designator \
 	-Wno-error=reorder-init-list \
-	-Wno-missing-include-dirs
+	-Wno-missing-include-dirs \
+	-Wno-reserved-identifier
 
 # Hand-written sign conversion diagnostics are resolved, but the
 # auto-generated ones need mig and iig to be updated to fix.  Disable the
